  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nTotal calculators = 120\n\n50 at ₹625.50, 70 at ₹712.80\n\nStorage cost = 6%\n\n40 cheap at +15%, 10 cheap at −10%\n\n70 costly at +12%\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nTotal CP = Purchase + extra cost\n\nSP = CP × (1 ± %)\n\nProfit% = (Profit / Total CP) × 100\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ CP (cheap) = 50 × 625.50 = 31275\n\n⇒ CP (costly) = 70 × 712.80 = 49896\n\n⇒ Total CP = 31275 + 49896 = 81171\n\n⇒ Storage = 6% of 81171 = 4870.26\n\n⇒ Net CP = 81171 + 4870.26 = 86041.26\n\n⇒ SP (40 cheap @15%) = 40 × 625.50 × 1.15 = 28773\n\n⇒ SP (10 cheap @10% loss) = 10 × 625.50 × 0.90 = 5629.5\n\n⇒ SP (70 costly @12%) = 70 × 712.80 × 1.12 = 55883.52\n\n⇒ Total SP = 28773 + 5629.5 + 55883.52 = 90286.02\n\n⇒ Profit = 90286.02 − 86041.26 = 4244.76\n\n⇒ Profit% = (4244.76 / 86041.26) × 100\n\n⇒ ≈ 4.93%\n\n**∴ Overall profit ≈ 4.93%**\n\n2f",
